- that women originated the norm;
- that women are its primary enforcers;
- that she benefits from it;
- or that men do not benefit from it elsewhere.

- trying to push away pain-related thoughts and feelings can increase pain or make it last longer;
- catastrophizing (assuming the worst) reliably increases how much something hurts;
- expectations change how strongly pain is felt, which is the basis of placebo and nocebo effects.
